{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And so it shall not be done</b> — to rape the virgins, for the nations fenced themselves off from forbidden sexual relations because of the Flood; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 34:7). And I do not know this, for the Canaanites were steeped in forbidden relations, in bestiality, and in male intercourse, as it is written (Leviticus 18:27), \"for all these abominations the men of the land who are before you have done,\" and they did not begin with them in that generation; and in the days of Abraham and Isaac they feared lest they kill them to take their wives. But \"and so it shall not be done\" is joined with \"in Israel,\" for a disgraceful thing he has done in Israel, and so it shall not be done among them; therefore he said \"in Israel,\" for it is not a disgraceful thing among the Canaanites. And Onkelos (Onkelos on Genesis 34:7) said, \"it is not fit to be done,\" to say that it is forbidden, and therefore it is a disgraceful thing in Israel:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "Rashi's interpretation referenced here appears in Rashi on Genesis 34:7; the phrase שטופים בעריות is a rabbinic idiom meaning \"steeped/immersed in forbidden sexual relations.\""}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:39:19.960378968Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}